message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "BESS revenue stack: what common modelling shortcuts cost, measured on GB market data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Jing"
    given-names: "Jiawei"
    affiliation: "Makuhari Development Corporation"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ibarapascal/bess-revenue-stack"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - battery energy storage
  - BESS
  - energy arbitrage
  - degradation
  - power markets
  - Great Britain
abstract: >-
  Measures how much five common modelling shortcuts overstate grid-scale
  battery revenue, one at a time, on a 50 MW / 100 MWh asset priced against
  Elexon half-hourly GB market data from March 2024 to January 2026. Pricing
  wear at zero overstates net revenue by 42-78 percent; omitting state-of-charge
  headroom for reserve by 3-15 percent; a real forecast captures 60 percent of
  gross margin but only 48 percent of net. A single flat round-trip efficiency
  turns out to contain two errors of opposite sign that largely cancel, and a
  single wear price across services shifts reserve holdings by 0.3-6.2 MW. Every
  finding is measured on the same asset over the same window.
